WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.100
- All right, how about this?

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.500
I will bet you that by midnight tonight

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.610
I can steal the Medal of
Valor from your office.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.880
- And this won't interfere
with you doing your job?

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.671
- You mean my job as an
amazing detective/genius?

00:00:11.671 --> 00:00:14.340
No it will not, I'll do
all of my work guaranteed.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.958
- I'm considering, I'm interested,
I agree to participate.

00:00:17.958 --> 00:00:19.350
(bell rings)
- All right,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.760
there's the robot I fell in love with.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.120
- You have five minutes
until your deadline.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.430
And here you are, handcuffed
to a table, in a locked room.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.263
- Which is precisely
where I planned on being.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.150
Captain, let me tell you a little story.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:34.950
You remember when I fell
through your celing?

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.230
- Yes, that was six hours ago.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.050
- It was, I admit, a disastrous failure.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.310
But it gave me the idea for Herman,

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.880
the friendly janitor you met.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.683
With Herman I commenced the perfect crime.

00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:48.187
- I caught you as Herman.

00:00:48.187 --> 00:00:50.201
- But you didn't catch Rosa.

00:00:50.201 --> 00:00:52.014
- [Raymond] Come out of there!

00:00:52.014 --> 00:00:52.847
(Jake sighs)

00:00:52.847 --> 00:00:54.450
- [Jake] As it turns out, our friend Rosa

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.343
is great at picking locks.

00:00:57.932 --> 00:00:59.270
- That does not surprise me.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:00.330
- No, me neither.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.830
Of course I had to find
a way to get her out

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.870
of your office without you seeing her.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.730
So I created a diversion.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.880
Not mistimed, perfectly timed.
(explosion booms)

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.573
So she could escape unseen.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:11.750
- What about the pigeons?

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.040
- Oh, the gray pigeons?

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.740
They were a red herring, thank you.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.850
Their only purpose was to
draw you into the copy room

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.320
while two members of my team
broke into your locked office.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.423
So now I had a way into your
office, and an open cabinet.

00:01:24.387 --> 00:01:26.670
All that was left was for the Royal babies

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:27.980
to steal your keys.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.960
- Yes, but you didn't need the keys.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.640
The cabinet was already unlocked.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.130
You needed a way into the safe.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:34.470
- And I got it.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.520
You were so concerned with
getting your keys back,

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:39.080
you didn't even notice the
Sergeant steal your phone.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.750
That's right, even the
Sergeant's on my side.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.940
I then had Charles dust your
screen cover for prints.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:45.250
The greasiest smudges revealed

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.320
the four numbers you use the most.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.410
The four numbers in your passcode.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:51.410
Based on your advanced age I assume

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.490
that you use the same
passcode for everything.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:57.020
Your phone, your email,
and of course, your safe.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.913
- That would be a fair assumption.

00:01:58.913 --> 00:02:01.700
- And as you walked over
here, Charles awkwardly

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.570
stuffed himself through your
window and opened your safe.

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.230
We had the four numbers of your code,

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.160
which meant there were
24 possible combinations

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.200
for Charles to try.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.380
That could take up to four minutes,

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.870
which is why I really
dragged out this explanation.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.360
I mean really stretched it.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.860
I don't know if you noticed,
but there were times

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.927
where I was like, "What
am I even talking about?

00:02:17.927 --> 00:02:20.600
"This isn't a," oh!
(watch beeps)

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:23.060
But, now, four minutes is up.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.810
Which means Boyle is
either on the other side

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.813
of that door holding
your medal, or I've lost.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.640
- Well Captain, it seems that Jake isn't

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.278
the only person you underest--

00:02:35.278 --> 00:02:36.111
(bell rings)

00:02:36.111 --> 00:02:38.058
- But now it's time for round
two of our Halloween bet.

00:02:38.058 --> 00:02:39.530
This year I believe I'll make things

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:40.720
more difficult for myself.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.230
Let's say, what, I'll steal
the watch right off your wrist.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.620
- My watch is right here.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.030
- No, I made a switch, that's a fake.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.840
- No, this one's a fake.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.050
- What?

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.180
No!

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.420
What?

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:56.600
No!

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.433
What?

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.790
No!

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:02.113
You were behind all this.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.760
You played me!

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:08.220
- Like Franz Bluheim plays the flute.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.620
- But how could you possibly have known

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.410
I was gonna try and steal your watch?

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.920
- I knew you would try to take
something important to me.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.204
During the year I drew
your attention to my watch

00:03:18.204 --> 00:03:21.020
You're eight minutes late.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.910
You're 14 minutes late.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.780
You're three minutes early.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.223
In Chicago.

00:03:27.323 --> 00:03:29.550
- You annoyed me into stealing it.

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:32.990
- Exactly, now you had a
target, but you needed a plan.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.500
Fortunately it walked through the door,

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.460
handcuffed to Diaz.

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.305
- Scumbag pickpocket is Stan McCreary.

00:03:39.305 --> 00:03:41.520
He can take anything off of anyone.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.780
- Anything, anyone?

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.280
- The look on your face, priceless.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.160
I put McCreary into my employ immediately.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.970
Fast-forward to this morning.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.320
You commenced your plan.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.250
McCreary stole my watch
and then replaced it

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:57.610
with a replica, and while you celebrated,

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:00.670
McCreary put my watch back in my pocket.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:03.110
The watch never left my person.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:03.943
Dun-dun-dun!

00:04:07.732 --> 00:04:08.640
(bell rings)
- Today is the most

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.900
important day in the
history of this precinct.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.310
For today is Halloween Heist
3: the Heistening, tagline:

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:17.130
- This year we both attempt
to steal the same object

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.750
instead of Jake attempt
to to steal one from me.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.400
- I gave you one direction
on the tagline, snappy.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.843
But yes, we will be attempting
to steal the same item, this.

00:04:25.826 --> 00:04:28.760
(funky music)

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.640
- I don't understand what is happening.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.040
- Allow me to explain.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.320
Amy and I were ahead
of you the whole time.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.270
- No, you weren't part of this.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.610
Get back over to the loser side, loser.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.650
- All right, worth a shot.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.196
- Remember when you set off the witch?

00:04:44.196 --> 00:04:45.029
(witch cackles)

00:04:45.029 --> 00:04:47.180
You made Captain Holt
flinch, which was weird,

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.640
since his door was closed, but not weird,

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.210
since he actually heard it over a bug

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:52.760
he planted at your desk.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:55.290
It was in an old muffin that
you never threw in the trash.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.900
- That's why people throw away garbage.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.039
- How are we together?

00:04:58.039 --> 00:04:58.980
- Eh.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.210
- Anyway, I tapped into
the bug's frequencies,

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:02.880
so I had ears on Jake.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.450
I needed to know what Holt was up to.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.430
That's where Hitchcock came in.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:08.570
- I masterminded the entire plan.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:09.880
- You did one small thing,

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:12.310
and I had to explain it
to you, like, 45 times.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:13.640
He left a tiny crack in the blind,

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.507
so I could read the Captain's lips.

00:05:15.507 --> 00:05:17.907
"Sharon and your kids will distract Jake.

00:05:17.907 --> 00:05:19.667
"They'll be here at 9:30 sharp.

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:22.658
"My waffle xylophone on the cheese man."

00:05:22.658 --> 00:05:23.491
- What?

00:05:23.491 --> 00:05:24.820
- My lip-reading is not flawless.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.340
Now that I knew your plan,
it was simple to disrupt.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.190
While Scully gracefully moved the witch,

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:30.600
I got into character.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.500
Holt triggered the witch, which
brought Jake into the room.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:35.370
- And I threw the crown in the trash can.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:37.053
- Exactly as I planned.

00:05:37.053 --> 00:05:39.246
- All hail the crown of destiny.

00:05:39.246 --> 00:05:42.410
(crowd cheers)

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:45.530
This year's Halloween Heist
is a three-way tiebreaker

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.460
to determine the champion of champions.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.737
We'll be playing for
this: a plaque that reads,

00:05:49.737 --> 00:05:52.177
"The Ultimate Detective/Genius".

00:05:53.369 --> 00:05:55.420
(dramatic music)
- 'Sup, losers?

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.357
I have the real plaque, unh, unh!

00:05:58.357 --> 00:05:59.640
It was all me.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:02.950
Three weeks ago, Captain Holt
asked me to order a plaque

00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:07.020
that read, "The Ultimate
Detective/Genius".

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:09.570
I did it, and I ordered three copies

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:12.050
and a statue of Tyrese riding a dolphin.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:12.990
- Is that relevant?

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.640
- To my life, yes.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.650
- Once I had the plaques,
I manipulated Captain Holt

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:20.400
into choosing Boyle as his partner.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.340
All it took was six bottles of dish soap.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:25.090
See, this is what happens when Jake tries

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:26.710
to wash dishes by himself.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:28.828
It's like he's helpless without Boyle.

00:06:28.828 --> 00:06:33.427
- Yes, he is helpless without Boyle.

00:06:33.427 --> 00:06:37.320
- And you fell for my trap
like a greedy little rat.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:38.153
- Easy.

00:06:38.153 --> 00:06:40.370
- Yes, it was easy.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.181
And the next phase of my plan,

00:06:42.181 --> 00:06:45.120
a quote unquote, skating accident.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:47.240
- But you knocked out
your two front teeth.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.690
- False teeth.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.240
Fake blood.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.630
I lost my real teeth at Jen Sutton's

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:55.090
birthday party in fourth grade.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.010
Once I had faked the skating mishap,

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:00.130
I swapped out a dummy
plaque for the real one.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:02.100
I came back, wearing the perfect disguise

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:04.690
to make sure I was
never noticed by anyone.

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:07.570
Something so drab and uninspiring--

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.160
- This feels like it's
gonna be a dig on me.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:10.170
- I wore Amy's clothes.

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:11.003
- There it is.

00:07:11.003 --> 00:07:13.290
- This is your doing, you
and your male prostitute.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:15.880
- [Jake] Bill is not a male
prostitute, I don't think.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:17.160
- That suit is not drab.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.820
It has a fun salmon lining.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:20.760
- No, Amy, it made me invisible.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:23.500
And now that I had that
power, every time one of you

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:26.020
stole a plaque, I replaced it with a fake.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:29.240
And no one had any idea
until the lights went out,

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:32.290
revealing a secret
message, "Heists are dumb".

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:35.340
And now here you all are, locked up

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:38.580
behind the glass like
a bunch of loser fish.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:43.210
- [All] Gina Linetti is
the ultimate human/genius.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:44.043
- Thank you.
(bell dings)

00:07:44.043 --> 00:07:45.110
- This year, we compete for the most

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.670
elegant and regal of all prizes.

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:49.490
- A championship cummerbund.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.140
- Or belt, as normal people call it.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:54.810
This heist, the belt will not
be locked up or hidden away.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:57.360
It will be suspended from
the ceiling in plain sight

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.270
for all to see.

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:00.980
- How poetic, it will
hang just out of reach,

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.264
like Tantalus's fruit.

00:08:03.264 --> 00:08:05.530
- [Jake] What's going
on, what's happening?

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:06.363
- [Charles] I can't see!

00:08:06.363 --> 00:08:07.850
- [Hitchcock] Everybody
just grab something random.

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:09.130
- [Rosa] Back off Hitchcock.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.740
- Silence!

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:12.790
It's gone, the cummerbund is gone!

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:13.916
- Hello, Jacob.

00:08:13.916 --> 00:08:16.570
- (yells) What, Ames,
what are you doing here?

00:08:16.570 --> 00:08:17.800
Why aren't you out looking for the belt?

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.950
- You and I both know the
belt never left the precinct.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:21.480
- I don't know that, nobody knows that.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.890
- I kept thinking, "How
did anyone swap my key?"

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.940
And then it hit me, they didn't.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.260
They swapped the safe.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.409
One of the handmaids, I'm
assuming fake Charles,

00:08:29.409 --> 00:08:33.816
took my safe, and then
Ofamy deposited a lookalike.

00:08:33.816 --> 00:08:36.020
What did you give fake
Charles so he'd help you?

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:37.760
- Nothing, in fact, he gave me something,

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:39.800
the power of financial freedom.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:41.310
I invested in a pyramid scheme.

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:42.350
No time to go into it right now.

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:44.850
- Okay so, while we
all tried to figure out

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:47.850
who had the real key, fake
Charles broke into the safe,

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.800
removed the tracker, and led
Terry and the whole squad

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.370
on a wild goose chase.

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:54.360
My only question is,
which box is the belt in?

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:56.130
- Well, good luck figuring it out,

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.590
because the clock is tick-tick-tocking.

00:08:58.590 --> 00:08:59.423
- It's that one.

00:08:59.423 --> 00:09:00.256
- No!

00:09:00.256 --> 00:09:02.560
- The dust pattern on top
doesn't match its neighbors.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.280
You see, Jake, I'm always
gonna be one step ahead of you.

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:07.220
You've lost the ability to surprise me.

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:09.080
Ya just plain boring.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:11.740
- Again, weird take on a
very loving relationship.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:16.428
- And it's midnight, so I guess
I'm an amazing human/genius.

00:09:16.428 --> 00:09:19.570
- You might wanna read the
inscription on that there belt.

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:22.808
- Why, oh, no, what does it say?

00:09:22.808 --> 00:09:25.999
"Amy Santiago, will you marry me?"

00:09:25.999 --> 00:09:28.200
- Will you marry me?

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.495
- Jake Peralta, I will marry you.

00:09:30.495 --> 00:09:35.495
(Jake sighs in relief)
(gentle music)

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:39.163
- Jake and Amy.

00:09:39.163 --> 00:09:40.340
- [All] To Jake and Amy!

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:41.440
- Great stuff, great stuff.

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.470
So, since Peralta altered the cummerbund,

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.340
no one really won the heist this year.

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:46.730
Is that what everyone's thinking?

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:47.563
- Captain.

00:09:47.563 --> 00:09:48.780
- Right, right, sorry, not the time.

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:50.270
I'm so happy for you both.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.651
Technically, there was no winner.

00:09:51.651 --> 00:09:54.068
(bell rings)

